}
\section{Method}{

For each requested interaction effect, \code{\link[=ginteff]{ginteff()}} builds a
counterfactual hypercube of \code{2^k} "vertices" over the interacted
variables, calls \code{\link[marginaleffects:predictions]{marginaleffects::avg_predictions()}} to get one
average prediction per vertex with the user's chosen \code{vcov}, and
then forms the signed difference-of-differences linear combination
manually (using the per-vertex variance-covariance from
\code{\link[stats:vcov]{stats::vcov()}} on the predictions object). For partial-derivative
effects the result is divided by \verb{(2h)^k} analytically; for first
differences the divisor is 1.

Bypassing \code{\link[marginaleffects:hypotheses]{marginaleffects::hypotheses()}} lets us (a) apply the
cross-partial scaling exactly without numeric-derivative blow-up at
small \code{h}, and (b) pass through arbitrary \verb{vcov =} specifications
(\code{"HC3"}, \code{~cluster}, sandwich matrices) to the final SE.
}

